\ ==== locals ====

\ Word locals: the head list names what the body receives from the stack, and
\ everything else is declared where `to` first assigns it. Covers capture order,
\ implicit declaration, per-scope frames, the redundant spellings, `?` logic-var
\ slots, and interaction with delimited continuations (shift/resume).

\ -- 1: one capture
: sq | x | x x * ;
5 sq . cr

\ -- 2: two captures, leftmost deepest
: hyp | a b | a a * b b * + ;
3 4 hyp . cr

\ -- 3: no head at all — the first `to` opens the frame
: staged 10 to origin  origin 3 * ;
staged . cr

\ -- 4: captures in the head, working values declared in the body
: scaled | factor | 10 to amount  amount factor * ;
3 scaled . cr

\ -- 5: a quotation cannot name an outer local; park the value and pick it up
: nest | x | x [ 10 20 30 ] [: 2 pick + :] map nip ;
100 nest . cr

\ -- 6: an inner quotation's own capture shadows the outer one
: shadow | x | [: | x | x x * :] 9 swap execute  x + ;
4 shadow . cr

\ -- 7: recursion — each call gets its own frame
: fact | n | n 1 < if 1 else n  n 1 - fact * then ;
5 fact . cr

\ -- 8: a local set before shift is read after resume (frame relocation)
: shifter shift ;
: worker | x | shifter  x * ;
: ex reset 7 worker ;
ex 3 swap resume . cr

\ -- 9: multi-shot — the same continuation resumed twice, local intact each time
ex dup  5 swap resume . cr
        6 swap resume . cr

\ -- 10: three captures — verifies (a b c -- ...) order
: combo | a b c | a 100 *  b 10 *  c  + + ;
1 2 3 combo . cr

\ -- 11: [: receives into a quotation's own slots
: nest2 | x | [ 10 20 30 ] x [: element outer | element outer + :] curry map ;
100 nest2 . cr

\ -- 12: the opening bar is optional when names precede the closing one
: sq2 x | x x * ;
5 sq2 . cr

\ -- 13: ^ names a global the body assigns; without it the name would be a local
variable tally
: bump | amount ^tally | tally amount + to tally ;
0 to tally  4 bump  5 bump  tally . cr

\ -- 14: a ? slot is not received — it holds a fresh logic variable per call
: unify-fresh | ?q n | q n ~ drop  q ? ;
7 unify-fresh . cr

\ -- 15: inlined into the caller's body
: inlinee | a b | a 100 *  b 10 * + ;
inline
: outer-inline  7 7 inlinee ;
outer-inline . cr

clear
\ === errors: an outer local is not in scope inside a quotation ===
: read-outer | x | [: x + :] map ;               \ (a read of the word's local)
: read-outer-quotation | n | [: a | [: a n + :] map :] map ;  \ (the enclosing quotation's local)

clear
\ === errors: the head is one list, at the head, and never empty ===
: two-lists | items | | total | 0 to total ;     \ (a second list)
: mid-body 1 . | x | x ;                         \ (a list, but after code)
: empty-head | | 1 ;                             \ (nothing to declare)

clear
\ === errors: a name must be declared before it is read ===
: reads-unknown never-stored . ;                 \ (only `to` declares)

clear
\ === errors: assigning a global needs ^, in either head spelling ===
: writes-global 1 to tally ;                     \ (no head at all)
: writes-global-barless n | n to tally ;         \ (barless head)
: writes-global-barred | n | n to tally ;        \ (leading-bar head)

clear
\ === errors: a compile-time word cannot name a local ===
\ the name would shadow the construct itself: a local named `to` silently
\ disables assignment for the rest of the body
: head-to | source to | source ;                 \ (in the head)
: head-lvar-case | ?case | 1 ;                   \ (a ?-marked head name)
: hoisted-if 5 to if ;                           \ (declared by `to`)
: index-to 0 3 1 do to loop ;                    \ (a do index name)

clear

\ ==== lambda sugar ====

\ A quotation head names what the body receives from the stack. The opening bar
\ is optional, so [: x | … :] and [: | x | … :] are the same head. A ^ name is
\ the enclosing global rather than a capture; a ? name is a fresh logic variable.
[ 2 3 4 ] [: x | x x f* :] map . cr
[ 2 3 4 ] [: | x | x x f* :] map . cr
3.0 [: a | a a f* :] execute . cr

variable scale
2.0 to scale
[ 2 3 4 ] [: x | x scale f* :] map . cr
5.0 [: n ^scale | n to scale :] execute  scale . cr

[: ?q n | q n ~ drop  q ? :] 7 swap execute . cr

clear

\ ==== multiline locals ====

\ Multi-line locals declarations and comments within them.
\ Exercises the input-refill path (a locals list spanning input lines)
\ and comment-skipping inside the locals scan.

\ (1) word locals split across lines, with \ and ( ) comments mixed in
: add3
  | a b        \ first two operands
    c |        ( and the third )
  a b + c + ;
1 2 3 add3 . cr

\ (2) quotation locals split across lines
: hyp2
  [: | p
     q |
     p p *  q q *  +
  :] ;
3 4 hyp2 execute . cr

\ (3) a comment containing a word identical to a local name must not
\ be read as a second declaration of that local
: sq
  | n         \ n is the value to square
  |
  n n * ;
6 sq . cr

clear
